{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Be ready for three days.</b> Its sense is for the third day. According to the plain sense he did not add even one day on his own. Now I give you two trustworthy witnesses, both in this book: it is written, \"and he gathered them into custody for three days\" (Genesis 42:17), and there it is written, \"and Joseph said to them on the third day\" (ibid. 42:18), and it is written, \"and within three days Pharaoh will lift up\" (ibid. 40:19), and there it is written, \"and on the third day, the day of giving birth\" (ibid. 42:20), and likewise, \"be ready for three days.\":"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Genesis 42:20 but the content 'the day of giving birth' matches Genesis 38:24 (not 42:20); the citation may be corrupt in the source or a scribal error, translated as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:55.466601206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}